cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use perfgate or its data, please cite it as below.
title: "perfgate: statistical detection of frontend performance regressions in CI"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Doroshenko
    given-names: Vyacheslav
    affiliation: MIREA – Russian Technological University
repository-code: https://github.com/SlavaDoroshenko/perfgate
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
keywords:
  - web performance
  - performance regression
  - continuous integration
  - Lighthouse
  - Mann–Whitney test
  - change point detection
abstract: >
  perfgate compares the lab page-load performance (FCP, LCP, TBT, CLS) of two
  versions of a web application in the same CI job, with interleaved loads and a
  one-sided Mann–Whitney test with Holm correction and minimum effect margins. The
  repository contains the tool (GitHub Action, GitLab template, Docker image, PR/MR
  comment, history dashboard), the experiment protocols and the analysis code; the
  raw measurements are on the data branch.
